WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.099
Observed frequency divided by number of trials is experimental probability; it

00:00:05.099 --> 00:00:07.325
approaches theory with more trials.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:16.753
Write the observed heads frequency as a fraction: 59 heads in 120 trials. The answer

00:00:16.753 --> 00:00:23.025
is 59/120. Experimental probability equals observed heads divided by total tosses

00:00:23.025 --> 00:00:27.016
equals 59/120; it may differ from 1/2.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:34.493
In a probability experiment on a football field, a coin landed heads 32 times in 50

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:39.049
tosses. What is the experimental probability before simplification? Pause to choose

00:00:39.049 --> 00:00:39.877
and explain.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:48.310
In a probability experiment on a football field, a coin landed heads 32 times in 50

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:53.542
tosses. What is the experimental probability before simplification? The answer is

00:00:53.542 --> 00:00:58.774
32/50. Experimental probability equals observed heads divided by total tosses equals

00:00:58.774 --> 00:01:01.628
32/50; it may differ from 1/2.
